## 2. HOW TO DEFINE TOOLS

### Option 1: Using AIFunctionFactory with Delegates
```csharp
// Define a .NET method
private static string GetWeather(string location)
{
    return $"Weather in {location}: Sunny";
}

// Create an AIFunction
var weatherFunction = Microsoft.Extensions.AI.AIFunctionFactory.Create(
    delegate: new Func<string, string>(GetWeather),
    name: "get_weather",
    description: "Get weather for a location",
    serializerOptions: null  // Uses default
);

// Create AITool from the function
var weatherTool = new Microsoft.Extensions.AI.AITool { ... };

// Add to ChatOptions
var chatOptions = new Microsoft.Extensions.AI.ChatOptions
{
    Tools = new[] { weatherTool }
};
```

### Option 2: Using AIFunctionFactory with MethodInfo
```csharp
var method = typeof(MyClass).GetMethod(nameof(MyClass.GetWeather));
var function = Microsoft.Extensions.AI.AIFunctionFactory.Create(
    method: method,
    instance: myClassInstance,  // For instance methods
    name: "get_weather",
    description: "Get weather information"
);
```

### Option 3: Create AIFunction Declarations Only (No Invocation)
```csharp
var declaration = Microsoft.Extensions.AI.AIFunctionFactory.CreateDeclaration(
    name: "get_weather",
    description: "Get the weather",
    inputJsonSchema: jsonSchema,
    outputJsonSchema: null
);
```

### Tool Registration with Agent
```csharp
var agent = new Microsoft.Agents.AI.ChatClientAgent(
    chatClient,
    "instructions",
    tools: new[] { weatherTool, anotherTool }  // Pass tools here
);
```

